&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simone Bitton, 2021, 99 min. In Arabic, French and English with English Subtitles&lt;br /&gt;
Q&amp;amp;A with Madeleine Dobie&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Arabic, Ziyara (زيارة) means visit to the saints. Celebrated filmmaker Simone Bitton embarks on a personal road trip across Morocco, tracing the remnants of the country&amp;rsquo;s once-thriving Jewish community. In the 1950s, Morocco was home to 300,000 Jews; today, only a small fraction remain, yet their saints&amp;rsquo; tombs endure&amp;mdash;cared for by Muslim guardians who preserve their memory. Through close examination of synagogues, shrines, and village records, Bitton uncovers stories of coexistence, loss, and endurance. Ziyara is both a meditation on migration and a hopeful reflection on shared heritage, revealing a delicate thread between past and present, tradition and modernity. As the camera gathers stories, smiles, and blessings, it patiently repairs connections long thought severed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Watch the trailer &lt;a href="https://youtu.be/tyN85HpaMRs?si=l5U-RN4iU5QyL3Qc"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Join us on April 16 in-person or online via Zoom!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In a moment of AI hype and fatigue, the real differentiator is not technical capability but human leadership. In this IKNS Seminar, Salesforce CIO Advisor Chris Pe&amp;ntilde;a will explore how emotional intelligence, intellectual honesty, and principled decision-making will define the next generation of tech leaders.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Artificial intelligence is advancing at extraordinary speed. Boards are demanding strategies, investors want road maps, and most professionals are quietly wondering what it means for them. Join Columbia&amp;rsquo;s M.S. in Information &amp;amp; Knowledge Strategy (IKNS) program and Salesforce CIO Advisor Chris Pe&amp;ntilde;a for our next IKNS Seminar. Chris will reframe the AI conversation away from tools and toward leadership. Drawing from his experience leading enterprise technology at scale, along with themes from his book D&amp;eacute;j&amp;agrave; Boom: Hype, Hope, and Human Intelligence in the AI Era, Chris will explore the human side of technological transformation as well as the career challenges facing the next generation of professionals in an AI-driven world.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
The seminar will discuss why emotional intelligence matters more than technical fluency in moments of disruption, how leaders can guide teams without overhyping or underestimating AI, and why curiosity, courage, and intellectual honesty remain the foundation of durable careers. The central question is not whether AI will change everything, but who we must become as leaders in order to guide that change responsibly.&lt;br /&gt;
