&lt;p&gt;Columbia Pre-Law Society is proud to host Columbia&amp;rsquo;s first-ever Undergraduate Legal Conference! A&amp;nbsp;full-day event designed to bring students face-to-face with the realities, opportunities, and impact of a career in law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Taking place on Saturday, April 18 from 10:00 AM to 4:00 PM, this conference will feature a dynamic lineup of speakers from across the legal field, including attorneys from top corporate and Big Law firms, professionals working in immigration and human rights, experts in criminal law, as well as current law students and admissions representatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether you&amp;#39;re considering law school, exploring different legal pathways, or simply curious about the field, this conference offers a rare opportunity to hear directly from those shaping and navigating the profession today. Attendees will gain insight into career trajectories, day-to-day experiences, and the broader social impact of legal work, all while building meaningful connections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to speaker panels and discussions, students will have access to free professional headshots, complimentary Red Bull, and the chance to network with peers and professionals in an engaging, accessible setting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tickets are $7 and include full access to all panels, networking opportunities, and conference perks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us for a day of conversation, connection, and clarity about what a future in law can look like.&lt;/p&gt;

